}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Data Coverage by State (Months with Data)**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def calculate_coverage(df):\n    total_months = df[\"Date\"].nunique()\n    coverage = df.groupby(\"State\")[\"Date\"].nunique().reset_index(name=\"months_with_data\")\n    coverage[\"pct_complete\"] = (coverage[\"months_with_data\"] / total_months * 100).round(1)\n    return coverage.sort_values(\"pct_complete\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.795536Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.795873Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.801304Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.795848Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.800367Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":262},{"cell_type":"code","source":"coverage = calculate_coverage(df)\n\nprint(coverage.head(10))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.802451Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.802804Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.912432Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.802766Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.91152Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"          State  months_with_data  pct_complete\n14    Louisiana               101          31.2\n39        Texas               227          70.1\n3    California               291          89.8\n18     Michigan               292          90.1\n42     Virginia               300          92.6\n13     Kentucky               303          93.5\n4      Colorado               324         100.0\n5   Connecticut               324         100.0\n7        Hawaii               324         100.0\n6      Delaware               324         100.0\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":263},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"*Data coverage varies across states. 41 of the 47 states have complete data (100%), while six states have gaps. Louisiana has the lowest coverage at 31.2%, followed by Texas at 70.1%. California, Michigan, Virginia and Kentucky are missing only a few months, with around 90% or more of their data available.*","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Recession Periods**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Recession periods\nRECESSIONS = [\n    (\"1990-07-01\", \"1991-03-31\", \"Early 1990s recession\"),\n    (\"2001-03-01\", \"2001-11-30\", \"2001 recession\"),\n    (\"2007-12-01\", \"2009-06-30\", \"Great Recession\")\n]\ndef add_features(df):\n\n    df = df.copy()\n\n    df[\"RecessionPeriod\"] = \"No recession\"\n\n    for start, end, label in RECESSIONS:\n        mask = (\n            (df[\"Date\"] >= pd.Timestamp(start)) &\n            (df[\"Date\"] <= pd.Timestamp(end))\n        )\n\n        df.loc[mask, \"RecessionPeriod\"] = label\n\n    df[\"InRecession\"] = df[\"RecessionPeriod\"] != \"No recession\"\n\n    return df","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.913457Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.913781Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.919566Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.913745Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.918668Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":264},{"cell_type":"code","source":"df = add_features(df)\n\nprint(df[[\"Date\", \"RecessionPeriod\", \"InRecession\"]].head(20))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.921834Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.922125Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T20:00:18.075409Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T20:00:17.922081Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T20:00:18.074372Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"         Date RecessionPeriod  InRecession\n0  1990-01-01    No recession        False\n1  1990-01-01    No recession        False\n2  1990-01-01    No recession        False\n3  1990-01-01    No recession        False\n4  1990-01-01    No recession        False\n5  1990-01-01    N